data.content:
The root cause is that **Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi 10.0 upgrades to Microsoft.OpenApi v2**, which has several breaking changes. Here's what changed and the fixes:

---

### 1. `OpenApiString` / `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` types removed
The `IOpenApiAny` hierarchy is gone. Use `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode` instead.

```csharp
// OLD: param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");
// NEW:
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

Add `using System.Text.Json.Nodes;` and remove `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;`.

---

### 2. `OpenApiSecurityScheme` references reworked
`OpenApiReference` was replaced by typed reference classes. Use `OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference`:

```csharp
// OLD:
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
{
    Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
};

// NEW (operation transformer context now exposes .Document):
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2", context.Document);
```

---

### 3. `Schema.Nullable` removed
OpenAPI 3.1 uses JSON Schema's type-based nullability. Use the `JsonSchemaType` flags:

```csharp
// OLD: property.Value.Nullable = false;
// NEW:
property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
```

Add `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;` (for `JsonSchemaType`).

---

### Fixed code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;         // JsonValue
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;        // OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference, JsonSchemaType

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2", context.Document);
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

**Summary of changes:**
| What broke | Why | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `OpenApiString` | `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` removed in v2 | Use `JsonValue.Create()` |
| `OpenApiReference` + `ReferenceType` | Replaced by typed reference classes | Use `OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference(id, document)` |
| `Schema.Nullable` | OpenAPI 3.1 uses JSON Schema types | Use `Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null` |
